ZE0 navigation unit machine skeleton (SH-4A, SH7785).

Adds the `-M ze0` machine for the Nissan Leaf ZE0 / Clarion QY-7204N
Windows CE 5.0 head unit.  Research skeleton only; not a hardware model.

Base: QEMU 8.2.7 (tag v8.2.7), the pin in tools/qemu-ze0/README.md.
Depends on (and is generated against the tree after): M8.A4 CCN patches
(m8a4-0001..0003) and M8.A5 boot-stub patch (0002-sh4-ze0-boot-stubs).
build.sh applies *.patch in LC_ALL=C sort order, so this file
(ze0-0001-...) applies last; its meson/Kconfig hunks assume the CCN and
ze0-stubs changes are already present.

Provides: sh7785 CPU, 128 MiB RAM at phys 0x08000000 (plus P1/P2 aliases),
SH4 CCN at 0xff000000 / arrays at 0xf0000000, one ze0-stubs instance, and
unimplemented-device catch-alls over P4 0xff800000-0xffffffff and areas
4/6.  No built-in loader (M8.A3); use -device loader as ce_qemu_probe.py
does.

TODO M8.A2.  Compilation/runtime against a built qemu-system-sh4 is
UNVERIFIED in this environment (missing glib-2.0 dev / no prebuilt
qemu-system-sh4); patch application is verified by git apply --check on
pristine 8.2.7 after the M8.A4+M8.A5 patches.

